{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04AY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\text{id} : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0003": "$M$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{enumerate}\n\\end{definition}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4d28449c82eb2cce59de000babb0ff91a460ea80ba0bb2f784e13bdca9ceb9c8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9b8bd09e43f28838bc5e560aa29d8d0619026cb35ef4156b665d0dd501695a86", "source_text": "We say that an index category <MATH_0001> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>codirected<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, or\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>cofiltered<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if <MATH_0002> is\ncofiltered (in other words you erase the <MATH_0003> in part (3) above).", "source_text_hash": "sha256:57dea9730f61400e3bdd6a0f73e901d79011e0fa19bcb938830bc1d685aadea2", "unit_id": "tag:04AY:p002"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04AY", "placeholders": {"QUOTECLOSE_0001": "''", "QUOTEOPEN_0001": "``", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-nonempty-limit}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\noindent\n", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:05426f9606518946c01c1e11689ee3c1df32eb120d4312489b3967c2b193ae4b", "source_text": "We observe that any diagram with cofiltered index category is cofiltered,\nand this is how this situation usually occurs.\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAs an example of why cofiltered limits of sets are <QUOTEOPEN_0001>easier<QUOTECLOSE_0001> than\ngeneral ones, we mention the fact that a cofiltered diagram of finite\nnonempty sets has nonempty limit (Lemma <REF_0001>).\nThis result does not hold for a general limit of finite\nnonempty sets.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:46252944b6af443cfc34d0e7560477ffe032899dafcad615cc7e6c50bb77eaf0", "unit_id": "tag:04AY:p003"}
